  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The websocket that updates the friends list & the list of worlds your friends are in remains connected so long as you do not switch pages. As soon as you go to any other page, the websocket disconnects & is not replaced. The only way to reconnect it is to refresh the page. This started sometime in early January. Prior to then, switching pages did not cause a permanent disconnect. \n\n\nIf the websocket closes under any *other* circumstances (it seems to time out naturally once an hour or so) a new websocket is successfully made to replace it, as expected.\n\n\nSteps:\n1. Start out on any page of the website.\n2. Click on anything that will cause a page switch. (a user, anything in the side bar, etc)\n3. The websocket is now disconnected & friends list / world list will no longer update without a page refresh.\n\n\nPictures of the websocket in the inspector's Network panel before & after a page change below.",
